  o Minor features (relay, denial of service):
    - Add a relay-wide bound on the number of tunneled BEGIN_DIR directory
      connections waiting for an HTTP request at once, enforced when the stream
      is admitted and paired with a deadline that reclaims a connection whose
      request never arrives. This complements the per-circuit BEGIN_DIR
      defenses from 0.4.9.15 by bounding the relay-wide population those do not.
      Controlled by consensus parameters, DoSBeginDirWaitEnabled,
      DoSBeginDirWaitMax, DoSBeginDirWaitTimeout and an observe-only mode
      (DoSBeginDirWaitObserveOnly) for calibrating the bound on live traffic,
      and disabled by default; the compiled thresholds are provisional. Closes
      part of ticket 41339.
